articles.content_en:
Article 65 In a financial leasing contract, if the lessee fails to pay the rent as agreed and still does not pay within a reasonable period after receiving a demand for payment, and the lessor requests the lessee to pay all remaining rent and to be satisfied from the proceeds of auction or sale of the leased property, the People's Court shall support such a request; if a party requests that the rent be paid from the proceeds of auction or sale of the leased property by referring to the relevant provisions of the Civil Procedure Law on "cases for realizing security interest," the People's Court shall permit such request.
If the lessor requests to rescind the financial leasing contract and recover the leased property, and the lessee, by way of defense or counterclaim, argues for the return of the value of the leased property exceeding the overdue rent and other expenses, the People's Court shall handle the matter together. If the parties dispute the value of the leased property, the value shall be determined in accordance with the following rules:
(1) if the financial leasing contract stipulates a method, it shall be followed;
(2) if the financial leasing contract does not stipulate a method or the stipulation is unclear, it shall be determined based on the agreed depreciation of the leased property and the residual value of the leased property upon the expiration of the contract;
(3) if the value is still difficult to determine pursuant to the methods stipulated in items (1) and (2), or if a party considers that the value determined pursuant to the methods stipulated in items (1) and (2) seriously deviates from the actual value of the leased property, an appraisal shall be conducted by a qualified institution commissioned upon the party's application.
